{"baseRefOid":"efd29c05204703acca9a0860812f54b94fae54b1","body":"## Disposition\nUnsolved after five substantive author turns. The original broader growth question and the explicitly labeled finite-prefix quantity M(D) remain unresolved. The unrestricted infinite-set supremum is infinite almost surely by a credited prior-result corollary; that literal observation is not the quantitative resolution.\n\n## Reviewed partial results\n- Almost-sure annular amplification of the credited FGK polylogarithmic lower bound, deterministic extended liminf/sup exponents, and fixed-cardinality stabilization\n- A uniform diagonal-flag argument proving limsup log M(D)·log log D/log D ≤ (log 3−1)(log 2)^2 almost surely\n- Polynomial raw q>1 moment lower bounds, including liminf E[M(D)^2]/D ≥ 1/96, with rare-tail and logarithmic-moment statements kept distinct\n\nThe upper scale remains far above a polylogarithmic bound. No sharp prefix exponent, convergence on the log-log scale, original-question counterexample, or complete solution is claimed. FGK's published inputs and method receive credit. The recent Mao–Song v2 preprint is not fully independently audited or used to infer the prefix exponent; divisor results are not transferred without proof.\n\n## Preservation and verification\nAll 42 frozen author files and eight independent review files are unchanged. Three additive publication files provide scope and portable verification. The author checkpoint cd4f8dc65cd68c002e2cf85c9df60ce962f33c0d is retained as the second parent of a fresh-main integration. Only this target folder and its own QUEUE status/turn cells change.\n\n150,925 author assertions and 8,390 independent exact controls pass; finite checks support the written proofs and do not prove limiting assertions. Work and review are AI-assisted, not a peer-reviewed publication or novelty certification. Raw source PDFs are linked/hash-bound rather than redistributed. Draft only; no merge or release.","files":[{"path":"unsolved_ma